✗ component declared but never built

    module "notification" (warren/boot_register_test.go:877)
      └─ warren.Providers lists warren_test.newDeadSubscription, which takes the lifecycle —
           and nothing in the module depends on *warren_test.deadSubscription.

  A provider nothing consumes is never constructed. Taking the lifecycle
  is a declaration that this component has work to do at start and stop,
  and that work will not happen: the hook is never appended, a consumer
  never subscribes, and the app logs a clean boot with /readyz green.

      warren.Eager[*warren_test.deadSubscription]()

  If something really should depend on it, make that dependency explicit
  instead — or export it, if the consumer is in another module. If it is
  dead code, delete it: this refuses to boot either way.